Rule 3 (replacement tensor dimensions must either match input tensor dimensions or equal 1 for broadcasting)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = shape(v_1, i) ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1
>>
Rule 4 (all replacement tensors must have matching number of dimensions with input tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_3)
>>
Rule 7 (replacement tensor must be broadcast-compatible with input tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_2) = 0 ∨ (ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = shape(v_1, i))
>>
Rule 9 (neginf replacement float value must be less than or equal to posinf replacement float value)
{v_1 : float, v_2 : float} |= v_1 ≤ v_2
>>
Rule 10 (replacement tensor rank must not exceed input tensor rank)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_2) ≤ ndim(v_1)
